CORE
main.c
--unwindset z_f.0:1 -- --apply-loop-contracts _ --no-standard-checks
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
--
The do-while(0) loop of z_f is unwound once by a first goto-instrument run,
then loop contracts are applied by a second one. The loop of a_acq has no
assigns clause and calls m_spin, whose loop has a contract. Inferring the
assigns clause of the outer loop must use a may-alias analysis that is
recomputed after the inner loop was instrumented; with a stale analysis the
instrumentation aborted with a CHECK_RETURN failure in local_may_aliast::get.
